e, though the test tail I captured doesn't show the pass count.\n\n- **Chip window:** `RcqView.tsx` now reads the last 14 days instead of the reset-based window, and the share note reads as specified.\n- **Summed shares:** `expectedOptions` in `rcq.ts` sums every row's share per key at the chosen tier. A key with several labels is named by the key itself.\n- **Long tail:** archetypes under 2% share go behind an `Other (N)` button in `InputsCard.tsx`, and `Fewer` collapses them again. Any tail chip you've picked stays visible.\n\nThree behaviours the spec didn't pin down, which you may want to check:\n- **Count shrinks:** the `N` in `Other (N)` counts only the hidden tail chips, so it drops as you pick tail chips.\n- **No-share keys:** archetypes the chosen tier never saw have no share, so they land under \"Other\".\n- **Expansion resets:** the expanded state lives in `InputsCard`, so it resets if the card remounts, for example when you change deck.\n\nI did not run the other checks from `CLAUDE.md` (`ruff`, `pytest`, the real-log verification), since only the web files changed. I didn't open the page in a browser either.", "ttft_ms": 1472, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 105326, "uuid": "bdc002fe-dd50-452f-97f9-7aae9d1475c6", "ttft_stream_ms": 1130, "time_to_request_ms": 51, "first_content_frame_ms": 1131, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
